This folder contains the material I am producing while studying Real-Time Operating Systems (RTOS), with a focus on FreeRTOS internals.

My goal is to understand how an RTOS kernel is structured, how its core components interact (tasks, scheduling, lists, queues, timers), and how these mechanisms are implemented at a low level.

The documents here summarize what I have learned during this exploration and highlight the concepts, patterns, and design decisions that are most relevant for embedded systems development.
